# Data integrity and provenance

Guardrails: G-01, G-04, G-05, G-10, G-11, G-12

## Append-only history (G-10)

- Observations and resolution decisions are never updated or deleted in place.
- A correction creates a new version that references the one it supersedes, with reason,
  actor, and timestamp. The previous version stays queryable.
- Each dataset row is a historical observation, not a duplicate to be collapsed.

## Raw and normalized side by side (G-11)

- Keep the value exactly as disclosed, plus its unit/scale, plus the normalized value and
  the normalization rule version. Normalization never discards the raw value.

## Provenance (G-12)

- Every material fact links to its source document, filing identifier, source location,
  retrieval/extraction time, and parser or rule version.

## Unknown and missing (G-01, G-04, G-05)

- Store Unknown explicitly (nullable value plus a status), never as 0, an empty string, or a guess.
- A missing period, filing, BDC, or field is recorded as missing coverage, never as zero exposure.
- Coverage is asserted per aspect (`FILING_METADATA`, `FILING_HISTORY`); an unasserted
  scope is Unknown, not zero.
- Do not derive a field from unrelated fields when it is not explicitly disclosed.
- Facts absent from a newer retrieval of the same source are counted and audited, never
  silently deleted.
- Cross-source disagreements stay as separate values plus a validation failure; do not
  pick a winner.

```text
BAD : fair_value = row.value or 0
GOOD: fair_value = None, value_status = "unknown"  # and the gap stays visible
```
